# Production30 agent contract

**Canonical:** `docs/CINEYOU_MASTER_SPEC.md`
**Plan / phases:** `docs/CINEYOU_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`
**Progress:** `docs/CINEYOU_PROGRESS.md` (update after every meaningful phase)
**Architecture:** `docs/CINEYOU_ARCHITECTURE.md`
**API decisions:** `docs/CINEYOU_API_NOTES.md`

On a new session or when context is large, reread those five files. They are authoritative over chat memory.

## Stack (do not substitute)

Next.js App Router + TypeScript strict + Tailwind + shadcn/ui. Cloudflare Workers via `@opennextjs/cloudflare`. D1 + Drizzle. Better Auth. Private R2. Workflows for production jobs. Containers + FFmpeg for branding. Rapyd Collect first (ZAR and USD). No Supabase. No PostgreSQL-specific SQL. No video blobs in D1.

## Customer language

Never expose Seedance, Topaz, fal.ai, FFmpeg, inference, models, codecs, or Cloudflare internals to ordinary customers.

Say: Produce Commercial, Commercial Concept, Filming Your Commercial, Enhancing Your Footage, Adding Your Brand. Could a 55-year-old business owner understand it without phoning us?

## Non-negotiables

- No fake numbers, testimonials, payments, or generation results
- Buttons work, are disabled with explanation, or do not exist
- Server-side authorization on every mutation; workspace-scope every query
- Private R2; store object keys only; short-lived signed URLs
- 1 Ad Credit = 1 production; concept generation is free
- Seedance source is 480p / 30s; branding text is applied in post, never generated
- `AI_PROVIDER_MODE=mock` must not call paid filming / enhancement / branding APIs; real adapters still exist
- Commercial Concept may be independently live via `CONCEPT_AI_MODE=live` + `OPENAI_API_KEY`. That must not silently mock when the key is missing. Default `CONCEPT_AI_MODE` follows `AI_PROVIDER_MODE`.
- Consult latest official provider docs before implementing external APIs; log decisions in `CINEYOU_API_NOTES.md`
- After each phase: typecheck, lint, relevant tests, build/preview, fix, update progress
